{"id": "EUVD-2026-86118", "enisaUuid": "9c00cbbd-c451-3f12-bcf0-0cf9fca8817e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngfs2: move quota_init qc iterator increment\n\nMove qc++ from the loop body into the for-loop increment\nexpression in gfs2_quota_init().\n\nThis keeps iterator progression explicit and avoids mixing pointer\nadvance with duplicate-slot handling in the loop body.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:05:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T05:30:58", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04ec2f3b29b3c8a59950b8816b5ebc8ba052808a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21a50a9373adab35ffadf5cf59272dc99078170e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/942202677f8f2ee448a6a2feb06aeeaf520342e3"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97520", "GHSA-wwp5-47mj-chgr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1bc9e962-790f-31fd-9b76-fd526b30ea29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de0d95c26c41c1776e4d23b1a8b3f2bcfd1dae5f <04ec2f3b29b3c8a59950b8816b5ebc8ba052808a"}, {"id": "5f6fcaaf-0416-3b9f-af3b-28d802e8bc56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de0d95c26c41c1776e4d23b1a8b3f2bcfd1dae5f <21a50a9373adab35ffadf5cf59272dc99078170e"}, {"id": "7daf5679-aed5-3a84-8020-3f05b4747038", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de0d95c26c41c1776e4d23b1a8b3f2bcfd1dae5f <942202677f8f2ee448a6a2feb06aeeaf520342e3"}, {"id": "96208bc3-0ab3-3fee-bf60-ef9d5391bc06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ab7abb39-8f2c-33eb-b4d0-987987e3e3a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "ac9db004-8549-3a86-b231-6cba13d95004", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_ver